eBytes,selectedSampleRecords:selectedRecords,selectedPercentOfWholeCheck:100*selectedTotal/treeTotal},byAllocationSite:Object.fromEntries(bySite),partitions,consumers:[...consumers.values()].sort((a,b)=>b.estimatedSelfBytes-a.estimatedSelfBytes),sourceEvidence:[{lines:'6942-6946',meaning:'Map.lo/hi construct Tuple plus MNode.'},{lines:'7014-7023',meaning:'Map.get.go recursively rebuilds a path using Map.lo/hi; its self allocation is distinct from child self allocation.'},{lines:'12138-12140',meaning:'checker_arena.name evaluates Map.get on name_ids before invoking name.result.'},{lines:'12121',meaning:'checker_arena.name.insert calls Map.set; name-namespace ancestry alone must not label writes as reads.'}],boundaries:['These are cumulative statistical worker-isolate allocation estimates from one instrumented49 run, not exact bytes/object counts, retained memory, CPU cost, or predicted52 speedup.','Visible stack ownership is conservative: inlined/missing caller frames and opaque closures can leave ownership unresolved. The definite category is supported by recorded frames, not proof that every real name-read allocation was captured or attributed there.','Only the three requested allocation sites are partitioned, not all Map-family allocations, all descendants of a name call, or all Arena reconstruction.','Replacing a read may still allocate in IndexLookup.find/Map.bit/Option handling, and optimization can move allocation attribution. Attributed pre-change bytes are not an asserted removable-byte total.'],normal49Controls:{runs:normal,baselineVariation:control.overhead,frequencyEvidence:{normalRunsRecordedFrequency:false,priorSeparateProfileSnapshots:{before:{at:profileBefore.at,cpufreq:profileBefore.cpufreq,procCpuInfo:profileBefore.procCpuInfo},after:{at:profileAfter.at,cpufreq:profileAfter.cpufreq,procCpuInfo:profileAfter.procCpuInfo}},limit:'No readable cpufreq governor/current-frequency interfaces. /proc/cpuinfo MHz snapshots belong to the earlier instrumented profile, not the later normal49 controls; no sustained-frequency or equal-clock assertion.'},confounds:['Normal49 before/after compiled113.842s/119.665s, a5.12% shift; check92.813s/98.104s, a5.70% shift, despite unchanged compiler/runtime/corpus.','Affinity remained allowed0-11 rather than a pinned core. No CPU governor/frequency lock or CPU quota was imposed. Memory cgroups do not isolate CPU scheduling, thermal behavior, host/VM contention, or concurrent V8/GC threads.','Load averages are host-level snapshots, not per-core utilization or exact competing-process attribution. Existing records do not explain the observed baseline drift causally.','Same Node23/cgroup/full workload and output equality are required for52, but an isolated52 timing compared with old49 cannot remove temporal load/frequency confounding. No additional control/profile is launched by this analysis.']},evidenceSha256:Object.fromEntries(['profiling-quality49-check-compact.json','quality-counter49-diagnostic.json','profiling-quality49-environment-before.json','profiling-quality49-environment-after.json'].map(p=>[p,hash(p)])),preservation:{rawProfileWritten:false,heavyBenchmarkProfileOrBuildLaunched:false,permanentCompilerChanges:false,directoryBytesBeforeReceipt:Number(spawnSync('du',['-sb','.'],{encoding:'utf8'}).stdout.split(/\s/)[0])}};
